Subject: [PATCH] lna: an agent's engine ignores a site's saved local-network permission

In an engine the AI Bridge starts for an agent, the Shell sets Local Network
Access to refuse, with no prompt, a public page's requests to this computer
and the local network (permissions.default.{loopback,local}-network = 2, on
the default branch and locked for that run). In one of the user's own
profiles opened for an agent, a site the user allowed there keeps its saved
permission all the same: nsHttpChannel reads the site's own entry before any
default, and the prompt code reads it again (the front end's permission
check, a worker's saved permission). Its pages' requests to local addresses
were therefore let through in the agent's run (#570, R29).

With this, in such an engine (its environment carries NULAVIO_AI_WORKSPACE,
which workspace.py sets and the Shell reads too), a saved allow grants
nothing and a request that Local Network Access would ask about is refused
before it is sent. A saved deny still refuses. Nothing is written to or
removed from permissions.sqlite, so the user's permission is there as before
once the agent's run ends. Outside an agent's engine nothing changes.

Owner: Nulavio maintainers
Upstream: not applicable (the AI Bridge and its environment are Nulavio's).
---
--- a/netwerk/base/LNAPermissionRequest.h
+++ b/netwerk/base/LNAPermissionRequest.h
@@ -14,6 +14,13 @@
 static constexpr nsLiteralCString LOCAL_NETWORK_PERMISSION_KEY =
     "local-network"_ns;
 
+// Nulavio: whether the AI Bridge started this engine for an agent (its
+// environment names the agent: NULAVIO_AI_WORKSPACE, which nothing in the
+// browser can change). There a site's saved permission to reach this computer
+// or the local network grants nothing, and no prompt is shown: a request that
+// Local Network Access would ask about is refused.
+bool InNulavioAgentEngine();
+
 using PermissionPromptCallback =
     std::function<void(bool granted, const nsACString& type, bool promptShown)>;
 
--- a/netwerk/base/LNAPermissionRequest.cpp
+++ b/netwerk/base/LNAPermissionRequest.cpp
@@ -20,10 +20,19 @@
 #include "nsIOService.h"
 #include "nsIPermissionManager.h"
 #include "nsPIDOMWindow.h"
+#include "prenv.h"
 #include "xpcpublic.h"
 
 namespace mozilla::net {
 
+bool InNulavioAgentEngine() {
+  // launcher/nulavio_launcher/ai/workspace.py (WORKSPACE_ENV) sets it for the
+  // engines the Bridge starts: the AI Workspace and the user's own profiles
+  // opened for an agent. The Shell reads the same (NulavioAgentNetwork).
+  const char* agent = PR_GetEnv("NULAVIO_AI_WORKSPACE");
+  return agent && *agent;
+}
+
 //-------------------------------------------------
 // LNA Permission Requests
 //-------------------------------------------------
@@ -149,6 +158,12 @@
 nsresult LNAPermissionRequest::RequestPermission() {
   MOZ_ASSERT(NS_IsMainThread());
 
+  // Nulavio: in an engine an agent drives, nothing below grants, neither a
+  // site's saved or temporary permission nor a prompt: refused, no prompt.
+  if (InNulavioAgentEngine()) {
+    return Cancel();
+  }
+
   // Enforce Permissions Policy for Local Network Access (Bug 1978550)
   if (!mLoadInfo) {
     NS_WARNING("LNA permission request without load info");
--- a/netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp
+++ b/netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp
@@ -2104,7 +2104,10 @@
   }
 
   // Step 1. Check for  Existing Allow or Deny permission
-  if (nsContentUtils::IsExactSitePermAllow(mLoadInfo->TriggeringPrincipal(),
+  // Nulavio: in an engine an agent drives, a site's saved allow grants nothing
+  // (its saved deny still refuses); LNAPermissionRequest then refuses.
+  if (!InNulavioAgentEngine() &&
+      nsContentUtils::IsExactSitePermAllow(mLoadInfo->TriggeringPrincipal(),
                                            aPermissionType)) {
     userPerms = LNAPermission::Granted;
     return userPerms;
